&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Global Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Strategic Partnerships Manager, Deliveroo Express&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Deliveroo, our mission is to transform the way people shop and eat, bringing the neighbourhood to your door by connecting customers, restaurants, shops and riders. We give people the opportunity to buy what they want, when and where they want it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a technology-driven company at the forefront of the most rapidly expanding industry in the world. We are still a small team, making a very large impact, looking to answer some of the most interesting questions out there. We move fast, value autonomy and ownership, and we are always looking for new ideas.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits within the New Verticals business unit on our Global Strategy, Product and Commercial team, reporting into the Head of Strategic Partnerships, Deliveroo Express with our broader team reporting up into the Director, GM of Drive EMEA and VP of EMEA Markets. We are responsible for setting the strategy and lighting up new verticals, ensuring that Deliveroo has the right to win in the new and highly competitive on-demand Grocery and Retail market. The culture within the&amp;nbsp; team is informal, fast-paced and entrepreneurial. Given the growth of the business and the senior stakeholder exposure, progression in the team can be fast.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deliveroo Express is Deliveroo’s white-label solution that allows our partners to offer on-demand delivery directly through their own online websites / apps. Imagine going onto your favourite restaurant, grocer or retailers’ website and having an order delivered in as little as 20 minutes - from the customer’s point of view, you’re ordering directly with the restaurant / grocery / retailer, and it’s simply delivered by our rapid riders. For more, please see: &lt;a href=&quot;https://merchants.deliveroo.com/what-we-offer/deliveroo-express&quot;&gt;https://merchants.deliveroo.com/what-we-offer/deliveroo-express&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Strategic Partnerships Manager in the team, you will manage the day-to-day relationships with our white-label partners, which includes leading regular performance reviews, identifying opportunities for growth and overcoming operational challenges. You will work closely with various functions of Deliveroo to share insights from partners and ensure we are developing a “best in class” value proposition. With Deliveroo Express being a new product launched in April, you will play a pivotal role in defining the on-going strategy and driving success of this proposition.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Using data to understand trends in performance and identify opportunities for operational excellence will be critical to your success in the role. You will need to be able to manage multiple projects at once, interacting with key functions such as Product, Operations and Commercial. You will use your business acumen and negotiation skills to win new business deals and build an on-going pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working with partners of this scale, you will often overcome challenges that Deliveroo is facing for the first time, helping to shape the future of how we work with and scale our white-label partners.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Directly own the day-day relationship with Deliveroo Express partners across all verticals - Restaurants, Grocery and Retail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyse and present insights on performance against KPIs during weekly/monthly/quarterly meetings and reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct detailed analysis and extract insights to deliver operational excellence and identify ways to course-correct if needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to deepen and grow our partner relationships&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop on-going sales strategy for Deliveroo Express including pipeline development across markets, with support from your Commercial lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct new business pitching and commercial negotiation for new partners, with support from your Commercial lead&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualities We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;DECISIVE AND INFLUENTIAL: ​you should thrive in a fast-paced environment, and be comfortable with making fast decisions, even in times of ambiguity and based on intuition. You are comfortable making recommendations and communicating them across the business persuasively. More importantly, you must have a strong desire to galvanise action within Deliveroo, thinking about the big picture but also not afraid to get into the weeds of a problem to get things done.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;ANALYTICAL AND COLLABORATIVE: ​there will be some number-crunching involved, but your role will also be about stepping back – you’ll need to see the bigger picture and understand how your insights are aligned with the direction the business is heading in.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;COMMERCIAL: you will need to excel in building relationships with local commercial teams, and external partners and understand how best to bring our proposition to grocers and retailers. You will need to build a deep understanding of the Deliveroo P&amp;amp;L and operations of the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4-6 years’ experience in an account management, grocery/retail operations or strategy / strategic partnerships role.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Confident &lt;/strong&gt;in analysing data and extracting compelling and actionable insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong &lt;strong&gt;operational mindset &lt;/strong&gt;to identify opportunities for excellence and course-correct when needed&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner obsessed&lt;/strong&gt;, with effective relationship building, organisation and &lt;strong&gt;communication skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative team player&lt;/strong&gt; who is able to get the best out of the people around you. Able to work effectively with various teams and all levels of Deliveroo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced &lt;strong&gt;negotiator &lt;/strong&gt;within the ability to drive mutual value for both partners and Deliveroo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;London-based with a minimum of three days required in the office&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with FMCG / grocery / retailer e-commerce or last mile operations preferable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in working in a dynamic high-growth company is preferable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We’re committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you’ll have the opportunity to let us know once you’ve submitted your application. We’ll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited about making a real impact in a fast-moving marketplace and growing your career alongside ambitious, supportive teams, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;Beware of recruitment scams: DASH Brands will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about DASH Brands&#39; legitimate recruiting process at&lt;/em&gt; &lt;a class=&quot;_ymio1r31 _ypr0glyw _zcxs1o36 _mizu194a _1ah3dkaa _ra3xnqa1 _128mdkaa _1cvmnqa1 _4davt94y _4bfu18uv _1hms8stv _ajmmnqa1 _vchhusvi _kqswh2mm _2rkolb4i _ect4ttxp _syaz13af _1a3b18uv _4fpr8stv _5goinqa1 _f8pj13af _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _30l313af _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _9h8h12zz _10531ra0 _1ien1ra0 _n0fx1ra0 _1vhv17z1&quot; href=&quot;http://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&quot; data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot; data-is-router-link=&quot;false&quot; data-testid=&quot;link-with-safety&quot;&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em data-renderer-mark=&quot;true&quot;&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Global Structure&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we’re unlocking new possibilities as one global team.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Backend Engineer to help build and evolve our new Common case-management system, which powers support-case handling across DoorDash, Wolt, and Deliveroo.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own significant end-to-end initiatives across our backend services: case lifecycle, routing and assignment, queue management, case evidence and history, and migration from legacy systems. This is a hands-on role for someone who can turn ambiguous customer and operational problems into durable technical solutions, coordinate other engineers, and set the standard for reliability and craftsmanship on the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead one or more project-level Case Management initiatives, on your own or by guiding a group of engineers, from discovery and design through rollout, measurement, and operational ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build scalable backend services and APIs for case creation, routing, assignment, transfers, audit history, notes, attachments, and queue-management workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help deliver feature parity with legacy platforms while safely migrating traffic across DoorDash, Wolt, and Deliveroo.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make and own most technical decisions within your scope. Write project-level design documents covering how sub-features interact, identify dependencies and risks, and break work into parallelizable delivery plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scope ambiguous customer and operational problems, weigh long-term against short-term trade-offs, and design durable solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Operations, Support, Data, and other engineering teams to define the right problems. Shape the team roadmap through prototypes, data analysis, project proposals, and backlog prioritization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the coordination a project needs, such as status updates and dependency tracking, and escalate early to keep delivery on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enforce team-wide quality objectives: lead design reviews, calibrate quality metrics, and improve logging, monitoring, alerting, and escalation policies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as first responder or incident commander, model good incident practice, and turn what you learn into playbooks and backlog work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introduce and guide AI best practices for the team, including evals, data privacy, and review of AI-generated code, and take part in AI-powered projects when they are central to the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design reusable, self-serviceable solutions, and consider cost efficiency, including compute and AI costs, in key designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers through code reviews, design guidance, tech talks, and constructive feedback. Interview candidates, join sell calls, and take part in hiring events when the team needs them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-have qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong backend engineering experience, including designing and operating backend services, APIs, asynchronous workflows, and data models at meaningful scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in at least one modern backend language, and a record of writing exemplary code for the core functionality of key components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of complex, customer-facing or operations-critical projects from technical design through production rollout.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience breaking projects into parallelizable work, identifying dependencies and risks, and giving accurate estimates for yourself and others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience using AI development tools to improve productivity, while validating generated output for correctness, security, privacy, maintainability, and reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment: the ability to turn ambiguous workflows and user needs into simple, maintainable technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to collaborate across functions, bring the right stakeholders into decisions at the right time, and explain trade-offs clearly to technical and non-technical audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong engineering craft: testing, code review, observability, incident response, security, and operational readiness, with experience designing for reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working on systems with high correctness and auditability requirements, including traceability of decisions and changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A mentoring mindset and a record of raising team-wide engineering standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Go experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with migration from legacy systems, gradual rollouts, traffic shadowing, and feature-parity programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting internal tools or operational user interfaces from the backend side.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-volume, multi-region, or multi-tenant systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as an incident commander or in running an on-call rotation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI-powered features, including evaluation of model output.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What success looks like&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Delivers a major Case Management initiative with clear technical ownership, predictable execution, and measurable customer or business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improves the reliability, maintainability, and cost efficiency of the Common system while enabling safe migration from legacy case-management systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helps move support traffic onto the Common system without reducing case-resolution quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds solutions that other engineers and operators can confidently reuse and operate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Acts as a technical leader within the team: unblocks peers and partner teams, improves engineering decisions, influences the roadmap, and strengthens cross-functional execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We’re committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you’ll have the opportunity to let us know once you’ve submitted your application. We’ll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re excited about making a real impact in a fast-moving marketplace and growing your career alongside ambitious, supportive teams, we’d love to hear from you!&lt;/p&gt;
