&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 53, 142); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;About Baringa&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Baringa is a global consulting firm that partners with leaders to drive change and create value. With deep industry expertise, and enabled by advanced technology, the firm helps clients to deliver with greater confidence and certainty. With over 2,000 people across the UK, Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, the firm combines global insight with local understanding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The firm works across energy and resources, financial services, government and public sector, consumer products and retail, pharmaceuticals and life sciences, manufacturing, and technology, media and telecoms, with capabilities spanning strategy, transformation and operational excellence – all powered by advanced technology, data, AI and digital innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clients value Baringa’s collaborative approach and the way its teams integrate seamlessly – all working with a shared understanding of what matters most. The firm is known for its kind, curious experts who listen closely and care deeply about client success as they help clients transform energy markets, modernise financial platforms, expand telecoms and digital networks through advanced data analytics, enable digital services in government, and unlock growth in consumer sectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Certified as a&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Great Place to Work &lt;/em&gt;around the world, Baringa has been recognised by the &lt;em&gt;Financial Times &lt;/em&gt;in 22 categories of its UK Leading Management Consultants rankings, and by &lt;em&gt;Forbes &lt;/em&gt;for four consecutive years as one of the World’s Best Management Consulting Firms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(0, 53, 142);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Our Technology team are looking for an experienced Digital Transformation Portfolio Senior Advisor - 9 month FTC to join the team.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Senior Advisor in Digital Transformation Portfolio, you will work across Technology &amp;amp; Cyber and Business Enablement to turn complex business needs into well-defined, prioritised and deliverable change. The role combines business analysis, process improvement, project and change delivery, demand management and portfolio governance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will own and progress a varied set of initiatives from early discovery and scoping through planning, implementation and adoption. You will act as a bridge between business stakeholders and Technology &amp;amp; Cyber teams, bringing structure to ambiguity, coordinating specialist input and ensuring that proposed changes are practical, governed and aligned to agreed outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will also help improve the team’s portfolio and demand management processes, data and tooling, particularly ServiceNow and Azure DevOps, so that decisions and delivery are supported by clear, reliable information.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 53, 142);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;What you will be doing&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead discovery and scoping for technology-enabled and operational change, clarifying the problem, desired outcomes, scope, stakeholders, constraints, dependencies and measures of success.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather, analyse and validate business requirements through process analysis, data review and stakeholder engagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate business needs into clear delivery artefacts, including options assessments, process maps, requirements, user stories, acceptance criteria, scope documents and implementation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate processes, to define clear ownership, opportunities for simplification, automation or AI enablement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate stakeholders, product owners, project managers, technical teams and subject matter experts to maintain momentum, resolve blockers and keep delivery aligned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the technology demand management framework from intake and triage through assessment, prioritisation, approval and transition into delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support prioritisation and capacity discussions by providing structured information on business value, strategic alignment, risk, effort, dependencies and readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support portfolio-level reporting of initiatives including pipeline, capacity and benefits reporting, using data and trend analysis to surface delivery concerns and inform decisions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 53, 142);&quot;&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;Your skills and experience&lt;/span&gt; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience in business analysis, transformation delivery, project delivery or a blended role within large-scale technology or business transformation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying, validating and scoping technology-enabled improvement opportunities, including automation and AI-enabled change&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High ownership and accountability, with the ability to manage competing priorities, operate effectively in ambiguity and maintain momentum in a fast-changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with portfolio and demand management frameworks, prioritisation models, capacity planning and benefits tracking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A collaborative, kind and inclusive working style, with a continuous improvement mindset and a focus on delivering sustainable outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
